WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.753 --> 00:00:13.514
Jo stood at the parlor window watching Dan.

2
00:00:14.255 --> 00:00:18.337
He ran up and down the drive, leaping and turning somersaults.

3
00:00:22.339 --> 00:00:23.920
you training for a race?"

4
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:25.301
Jo called out.

5
00:00:26.522 --> 00:00:28.123
Dan walked over to the window.

6
00:00:28.143 --> 00:00:34.505
"No, I'm only He stopped to catch his breath.

7
00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:39.229
"I'm only working off my excess energy so I don't run away from here."

8
00:00:40.730 --> 00:00:42.171
He quickly corrected himself.

9
00:00:43.572 --> 00:00:51.477
"I mean, I'm grateful for all you've done, but sometimes "When I was your age, I almost ran

10
00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:55.480
away from home myself," Jo said with an understanding smile.

11
00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.724
"Run away if you must, Dan, but come back soon because I'll miss you."

12
00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:05.223
Dan was surprised by this unexpected permission.

13
00:01:06.724 --> 00:01:09.526
"Well, I guess I won't go just yet."

14
00:01:09.546 --> 00:01:14.190
"Good! Now let's think of another activity for you."

15
00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:17.312
Jo paused, deep in thought for a moment.

16
00:01:17.332 --> 00:01:24.979
"I know—how about driving into town every day before school to do my errands?"

17
00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.541
"Really?" Dan said excitedly.

18
00:01:28.561 --> 00:01:31.464
"You'd trust me with a horse and wagon?"

19
00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:34.300
"Of course.

20
00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.041
You're good with animals."

21
00:01:37.881 --> 00:01:41.662
So the next morning Dan took on his new responsibility.

22
00:01:43.403 --> 00:01:46.984
He was happy for a while, but a few weeks later, Mr.

23
00:01:47.004 --> 00:01:48.944
Bauer caught him fighting with Jack.

24
00:01:48.964 --> 00:01:53.386
"You know fighting is forbidden!"

25
00:01:53.806 --> 00:01:56.547
the professor said sternly, separating the boys.

26
00:01:58.027 --> 00:02:00.388
"We were just wrestling," Dan said to Mr.

27
00:02:01.292 --> 00:02:03.473
Bauer, but then he apologized to Jack.

28
00:02:04.794 --> 00:02:10.999
"You need another outlet for your energy, Dan," the professor said, "so come with me."

29
00:02:14.541 --> 00:02:19.544
Mr. Bauer took him to a place where several huge trees had fallen in a storm.

30
00:02:21.786 --> 00:02:27.570
Soon Dan was busy chopping wood, and the professor was explaining Dan's newest chore to Jo.

31
00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:34.178
"When he gets bored with that," Jo said, "I don't know what we'll do."

32
00:02:35.399 --> 00:02:40.563
But Jo didn't need to worry because Dan soon found something to amuse himself.

33
00:02:42.344 --> 00:02:47.688
One afternoon Laurie brought a young horse called Prince Charlie to board at Plumfield.

34
00:02:49.469 --> 00:02:55.314
At first all the boys were fascinated by the handsome creature galloping around the pasture.

35
00:02:57.595 --> 00:03:06.410
But eventually everyone grew tired of watching Charlie—that is, everyone but Dan, who visited Charlie every day with

36
00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:06.950
an apple.

37
00:03:09.932 --> 00:03:15.036
No matter where Charlie was in the wide pasture, he came running when Dan whistled.

38
00:03:15.056 --> 00:03:18.998
"We understand each other, don't we, fella?"

39
00:03:19.359 --> 00:03:21.780
Dan said, rubbing the horse's nose.

40
00:03:23.602 --> 00:03:26.604
Laurie often came to see how Charlie was getting along.

41
00:03:27.772 --> 00:03:31.575
"I'm thinking of trying to ride him," he said to Dan during one visit.

42
00:03:33.117 --> 00:03:35.639
"He's young, but I don't think it will take much work to tame him."

43
00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:42.565
"He lets me lead him, but I don't think he'll tolerate anyone putting a saddle on him," Dan

44
00:03:42.605 --> 00:03:48.149
replied. "Oh, I'll tumble off at first, but Charlie will quickly get used to a rider."

45
00:03:50.011 --> 00:03:54.094
As Laurie walked away, Dan found himself staring at the horse.

46
00:03:54.114 --> 00:04:01.112
"Hmm. I wonder what Charlie would do if somebody tried to ride him," he thought.

47
00:04:03.414 --> 00:04:08.358
The longer Dan studied Charlie, the more obsessed he became with riding the horse.

48
00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.003
Sitting on the fence one day, Dan held out an apple.

49
00:04:16.685 --> 00:04:21.389
As Charlie nibbled away, Dan quietly slipped onto the horse's back.

50
00:04:22.651 --> 00:04:26.825
With an astonished snort, Charlie reared and threw Dan to the ground.

51
00:04:27.886 --> 00:04:31.207
The fall didn't hurt Dan, who jumped up and laughed.

52
00:04:31.227 --> 00:04:35.369
"Come here, Charlie, and let's try that again!"

53
00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.650
But Charlie refused to approach him.

54
00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.612
"I'll ride you yet!"

55
00:04:41.992 --> 00:04:42.752
Dan vowed.

56
00:04:43.993 --> 00:04:47.334
This was exactly the kind of challenge that appealed to him.

57
00:04:48.815 --> 00:04:50.796
The next day Dan tried again.

58
00:04:52.544 --> 00:04:58.048
The horse tried to buck Dan off, but Dan held on until Charlie started galloping.

59
00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:02.011
This time Dan landed hard on the ground.

60
00:05:03.372 --> 00:05:06.754
He lay still while Charlie tore around the field.

61
00:05:09.416 --> 00:05:12.798
After a few minutes, the horse cautiously approached Dan.

62
00:05:14.439 --> 00:05:21.104
Charlie sniffed the boy, who looked up and said, "You think you've beaten me, but you're mistaken."

63
00:05:23.508 --> 00:05:29.910
The following day Dan strapped a folded blanket to Charlie's back and let him race and rear.

64
00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:34.531
After a few more days, Dan was able to sit on Charlie.

65
00:05:36.312 --> 00:05:41.113
Every day after that, he managed a short ride before Charlie threw him.

66
00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:49.875
"I wish I could try a real saddle and bridle on you," Dan said, "but I'm afraid to

67
00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.796
tell anyone that I've been riding you."

68
00:05:53.296 --> 00:05:56.658
Little did Dan realize that Silas had been watching them.

69
00:05:56.678 --> 00:06:01.000
"Do you know that Dan's been trying to ride Mr.

70
00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:01.841
Laurence's horse?"

71
00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:03.361
Silas asked Mr.

72
00:06:03.401 --> 00:06:04.302
Bauer that evening.

73
00:06:04.322 --> 00:06:08.084
"He kept coming back from the pasture all black and blue.

74
00:06:08.124 --> 00:06:09.945
So I figured I'd keep an eye on him."

75
00:06:09.965 --> 00:06:12.686
"What?" Mr.

76
00:06:12.726 --> 00:06:13.407
Bauer said.

77
00:06:13.427 --> 00:06:17.869
"That sounds dangerous—you should have stopped him, Silas!"

78
00:06:17.889 --> 00:06:21.171
"But he was making progress with that horse.

79
00:06:21.731 --> 00:06:22.972
You should see them together."

80
00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:28.906
When the professor and Laurie confronted Dan, he confessed at once.

81
00:06:30.887 --> 00:06:34.348
Then he proudly showed them what he had accomplished with Charlie.

82
00:06:34.368 --> 00:06:41.671
"Thanks to your patience and perseverance, Charlie looks ready for a saddle," Laurie said to Dan.

83
00:06:41.691 --> 00:06:45.553
"Let me train him some more, and then you may ride him whenever you want."

84
00:06:48.294 --> 00:06:54.501
The other boys were jealous that Dan had made a pet of Charlie, but Jo admired what he'd

85
00:06:54.541 --> 00:06:59.163
done. She liked to lean on the fence and watch him work with the horse.

86
00:06:59.183 --> 00:07:06.286
"Charlie's a much nicer animal than the one who used to run wild," Jo said.

87
00:07:06.306 --> 00:07:12.288
"I'm taming a young horse myself, and I hope I'll succeed one day too."

88
00:07:14.849 --> 00:07:18.151
Dan laughed because he realized she was talking about him.

89
00:07:19.151 --> 00:07:24.515
Giving the horse a pat, he said, "We won't jump over the fence and run away, will we,

90
00:07:24.596 --> 00:07:25.018
Charlie?"
